   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am a student currently using evolutionary trees for risks analysis.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am working on visualisation of trees and find ggtree is a great package for plotting trees. But as a newbie of both R and bioinformatics, I cannot let it work properly. What I want to get are trees containing following information.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"><a href=\"http://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolibrary/images/evo/sixchars_phylo.gif\" style=\"margin-left:1em;margin-right:1em\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolibrary/images/evo/sixchars_phylo.gif&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482727736000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0an4jWzeoSjIimihm2Hb5e\"><img src=\"https://ci3.googleusercontent.com/proxy/0HB6sLvtoJity2yAb18zOKTN_FXlxesX4Dch73iUf13Dh7fNqyf2PW12CkV8baQ7mhwCqTQ3_vj6PUPLoDL6Q7MOXQVqrQpiLP7qAnx5erE9Q31rTgnFKBw=s0-d-e1-ft#http://evolution.berkeley.edu/evolibrary/images/evo/sixchars_phylo.gif\" border=\"0\"></a></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I work with binary data (0 for absence and 1 for the presence of a character), and the headers of columns are the characters (I want to annotate as these &quot;Vertebrae&quot;, &quot;Bony skeleton&quot; in the above graph), and the rows are different taxons. I use phangron to construct trees and hope to annotate the nodes (or edges) with the character(s) that made the bifurcations. It is similar to your example of “annotating tree with phangorn output”, but I cannot let it work properly.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">My code is as follows:</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#800\">#read file from local disk in csv format. **Currently transpose does not work, do not know why**</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>origin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">csv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">choose</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(),</span><span style=\"color:#000\">header </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> row</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">names </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>origin </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> t</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">origin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>events </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phyDat</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">origin</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;USER&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> levels</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#maximum parsimony to construct a tree **From official document, working properly**</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>dm </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">hamming</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">events</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>treeNJ </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> NJ</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">dm</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>parsimony</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">treeNJ</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> events</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>treePars </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">parsimony</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">treeNJ</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> events</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">#maximum likelihood to generate iniformation, **From <a href=\"https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/treeAnnotation.html#annotating-tree-with-ape-bootstraping-analysis**\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/treeAnnotation.html%23annotating-tree-with-ape-bootstraping-analysis**&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792482727737000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1D07GnynGyLkwEMN9P3uoP\">https://www.bioconductor.org/packages/devel/bioc/vignettes/ggtree/inst/doc/treeAnnotation.html#annotating-tree-with-ape-bootstraping-analysis**</a></span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> pml</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">treePars</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> events</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>fit </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pml</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optNni</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optBf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optQ</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>                 optInv</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optGamma</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">T</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> optEdge</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>                 optRooted</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">FALSE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;GTR&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br>phangorn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> phyPML</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> type </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;ml&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># plot tree **From same website, in section &quot;annotating tree with phangorn output&quot;**</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>ggtree</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">phangorn</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">+</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> geom_text</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">aes</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">x</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">branch</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> label</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">AA_subs</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> vjust</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=-.</span><span style=\"color:#066\">5</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span></div></code></div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Apologies in advance if this is a dumb question, and all comments are appreciated!</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Regards,</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Speed</p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p></div>"
    ]
